00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:10.600
- Good morning again, and welcome.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.420
I am Cynthia Roman,

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.260
Curator of Prints, Drawings, and Paintings

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.050
at The Lewis Walpole Library.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:16.960
for those of you who don't me.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.360
But I think I actually
know everybody out there.

00:00:20.296 --> 00:00:22.640
Thank you for being here this morning.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.900
I hope more people are
going to join us later,

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.283
recovering maybe from the
wonderful performance last night.

00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:33.623
These two days of "The
Mysterious Mother" programs,

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.930
have been part of a series of celebrations

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.033
sponsored by The Lewis Walpole Library.

00:00:39.889 --> 00:00:41.310
In this instance, partnering with

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.810
The Yale Center for British Art,

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.340
to celebrate the tercentenary

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.900
of Horace Walpole's birth,

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.090
which was actually last September 24th.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:52.923
I hope I got that right.

00:00:52.923 --> 00:00:54.020
I'm horrible with dates.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.633
Stephen, is it the 24th?

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.830
This is the last of
the series of programs,

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.900
that Jonathan Kramnick,

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.090
the Maynard Mack professor of English,

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:07.000
and Director of The Lewis Walpole Library,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.410
has conceived as the Walpalooza year,

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.350
and it was, it commenced appropriately,

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.780
and off that Strawberry Hill,

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.850
with the Walpole Wallow last fall.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.540
Events also included a mini conference

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.360
on the Castle of Toronto,

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.690
that Jonathon organized at
The Lewis Walpole Library,

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:28.542
and later in the fall, George Haggerty,

00:01:28.542 --> 00:01:32.353
distinguished professor of
English at UC Riverside,

00:01:32.353 --> 00:01:35.347
delivered a lecture on the many lives

00:01:35.347 --> 00:01:37.580
of Horace Walpole,

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:40.756
and led a workshop and
a round table on biography

00:01:40.756 --> 00:01:42.987
and queering archives.

00:01:42.987 --> 00:01:46.320
And we did an exhibition

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.640
and a two day conference
on "Global Encounters

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:50.840
and the Archives: 

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.723
Britain's Global Empire in
the Age of Horace Walpole"

00:01:54.723 --> 00:01:57.800
which was organized with Steve Pincus

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.993
and some Yale graduate students.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:06.820
I just want to say a particular
thank you to Jonathan,

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:09.010
for his strong support of the staging

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.290
of "The Mysterious Mother."

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:15.440
The idea has been growing
for a really long time.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.593
Years actually,

00:02:17.781 --> 00:02:21.810
and it's been embraced
with lots of enthusiasm

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.870
from so many at The Lewis Walpole Library.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.750
Fellows who have
contributed so essentially

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.560
their ideas and energies to
realizing these programs,

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.950
and I've had conversations with everyone

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.760
who has participated,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.280
and just to say, it's
really wonderful for me,

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.600
to be part of this community of scholars

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.260
and Walpole enthusiasts,

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.312
every single one of whom,

00:02:49.312 --> 00:02:51.670
from the very earliest notion,

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.670
responded with an unhesitating
and resounding yes,

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.020
I absolutely want to be part of that.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.253
So thank you all for that.

00:03:04.746 --> 00:03:07.800
I think actually, looking out there,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.710
everyone was part of the audience.

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:14.963
for the fantastic performance or staged reading

00:03:14.963 --> 00:03:18.400
of "The Mysterious Mother" last night,

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.470
